From: ashfordeOU <236818772+ashfordeOU@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:18:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] D17: D11c, the fusion-pnt timing bound adds the flicker phase
 variance accumulated since the last anchor (criteria 1, 2 and 4 met, 3 not
 met and recorded); D12 closed; RESULTS.md opens the bound's conservativeness
 as a new defect

Both suites (decoupled and the [coupled] stacked filter) add
clock.flicker_phase_variance_after_steps(steps since the last GNSS fix or re-sync) to the
phase bound; exactly zero without a flicker floor. The truth is not touched.

On fusion-pnt with the clock-ensemble floors, 200 runs at seeds 42 and 7
(docs/design/evidence/d17-defect-fixes/PREREGISTRATION.md):
1. integrity mean classical 0.99988 / 0.99989 (before 0.77101 / 0.75865, p05 0.508 /
   0.490), quantum 0.99896 / 0.99896; p05 1.0 throughout: MET.
2. without a floor, fusion-pnt and fusion-pnt-coupled give the bytes they gave before
   (compared byte for byte, then pinned as digests): MET.
3. pooled RMS(err/sigma) classical 0.768 / 0.783, quantum 0.590 / 0.592, band [0.8, 1.2]:
   NOT MET; the band is unchanged. The quantum clock is below it without a floor too
   (0.550 / 0.564: its bound carries the re-sync noise variance); the classical bound with
   the flicker term is conservative by about 1.3x because the filter re-estimates the
   frequency at each anchor. Recorded as an ignored test with the finding.
4. timing p95 and holdover means equal the pre-fix values; no shipped fusion scenario has
   a floor, so no golden moves: MET.

D12: closed in docs/design/evidence/d17-defect-fixes/RESULTS.md (no defect register
exists), citing acq-gridfree (VmHWM 213 MiB against about 30 GB); the defect D12 comments
in tests/iq_signal_matrix.rs now say it is fixed. The digest pins declare their scope.
